window.AEGIS_IC_MARKUP="<div class=\"ic-root\"><main class=\"ic-wrap\">\r\n<section aria-labelledby=\"icH1\">\r\n<p class=\"ic-eyebrow\">Impersonation Check · free · about 10 seconds</p>\r\n<h1 class=\"ic-h1\" id=\"icH1\">How easy is it to send email as your company?</h1>\r\n<p class=\"ic-sub\">Enter your work email and company domain. Your browser reads your domain's public mail records and shows how easy it is to send email as your company.</p>\r\n<form class=\"ic-form\" id=\"icCheck\" novalidate autocomplete=\"on\">\r\n<div class=\"ic-field\"><label for=\"icEmail\">Work email</label>\r\n<input class=\"ic-input\" id=\"icEmail\" name=\"email\" type=\"email\" autocomplete=\"email\" placeholder=\"name@yourcompany.com\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocapitalize=\"off\" required aria-describedby=\"icErr\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"ic-field\"><label for=\"icDomain\">Company domain</label>\r\n<input class=\"ic-input\" id=\"icDomain\" name=\"domain\" placeholder=\"yourcompany.com\" spellcheck=\"false\" inputmode=\"url\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" required aria-describedby=\"icErr\"></div>\r\n<div class=\"ic-hp\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><label for=\"icWebsite\">Website</label><input id=\"icWebsite\" name=\"website\" tabindex=\"-1\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div>\r\n<button class=\"ic-btn\" type=\"submit\">Run the check</button>\r\n</form>\r\n<p class=\"ic-err\" id=\"icErr\" role=\"alert\" hidden></p>\r\n<p class=\"ic-consent\">By running the check you agree that AegisAI keeps your email, the domain and the findings for 90 days to follow up where it is a fit. <a href=\"https://www.aegisai.com/privacy-policy\">Privacy policy</a>.</p>\r\n<p class=\"ic-cred\" id=\"icHint\">Public records only. Your browser sends the lookups to Cloudflare's and Google's public DNS services and to rdap.org, and never connects to your mail servers. From founders who led security products at Google, including reCAPTCHA.</p>\r\n</section>\r\n<ul class=\"ic-seq\" id=\"icSeq\" hidden aria-live=\"polite\"></ul>\r\n<div id=\"icOut\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\r\n<section class=\"ic-info\" aria-labelledby=\"icHow\">\r\n<h2 id=\"icHow\">How this check works</h2>\r\n<p>When you run the check, your own browser asks Cloudflare's public DNS service (Google's, if Cloudflare is slow) for the handful of records every mail server reads: who receives your mail, who may send as you, what to do with forgeries, and whether outgoing mail is signed.</p>\r\n<p>It then tries 16 lookalike spellings of your domain and asks whether each one is set up and can send email. For up to three lookalikes that can, it asks the public registration database (rdap.org) when they were registered.</p>\r\n<p>The check only reads public records. It never connects to your mail servers or to the lookalike domains.</p>\r\n<p>AegisAI keeps your email, the domain and the findings for 90 days, to decide whether to follow up.</p>\r\n</section>\r\n<section class=\"ic-info\" id=\"glossary\" aria-labelledby=\"icGl\">\r\n<h2 id=\"icGl\">Glossary</h2>\r\n<dl class=\"ic-gloss\">\r\n<dt>DNS (Domain Name System)</dt><dd>The public phone book of the internet. Anyone can read a domain's records, including attackers.</dd>\r\n<dt>MX record (mail exchanger)</dt><dd>The DNS entry that says which servers receive mail for a domain.</dd>\r\n<dt>SPF (Sender Policy Framework)</dt><dd>A public list of the servers allowed to send mail as your domain.</dd>\r\n<dt>DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail)</dt><dd>A signature your mail server adds to outgoing mail, checked against a public key in your DNS.</dd>\r\n<dt>DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting and Conformance)</dt><dd>The policy that tells receivers what to do with mail that fails SPF and DKIM: monitor, quarantine or reject.</dd>\r\n<dt>Gateway</dt><dd>A filtering product that receives your mail before Google or Microsoft does, such as Proofpoint or Mimecast.</dd>\r\n<dt>Lookalike domain</dt><dd>A domain spelled almost like yours, used to send mail that looks like it came from you. It passes SPF and DMARC because it is its own domain.</dd>\r\n<dt>Business email compromise</dt><dd>Fraud where an attacker writes as a colleague, supplier or executive, often from a lookalike domain or a hijacked real account, to get a payment or data.</dd>\r\n</dl>\r\n</section>\r\n<section class=\"ic-info ic-faq\" aria-labelledby=\"icFaq\">\r\n<h2 id=\"icFaq\">Questions</h2>\r\n<details><summary>What does AegisAI keep?</summary><p>AegisAI keeps your email, the domain and the findings for 90 days. The Impersonation Check reads public DNS records in your browser via Cloudflare, Google and rdap.org; we keep the work email you enter, the domain and the findings for 90 days to decide whether to follow up. Like any website, those DNS services see your internet address and the names looked up. Your browser also keeps a small daily count of checks, which never leaves your device.</p></details>\r\n<details><summary>Is this a security audit?</summary><p>No. It is a quick reading of public DNS records at the moment you run it, for information only, with no warranty. A clean result does not mean you are safe from impersonation, and a gap does not mean you have been attacked.</p></details>\r\n<details><summary>Why not a score out of 100?</summary><p>Scores invite arguments about weighting. The records are either set or not, and the honest answer fits in three words: basics in place, gaps in the basics, or open to impersonation.</p></details>\r\n<details><summary>Why does email signing say \"not found\"?</summary><p>Signing keys are published under names each company chooses. We look under the most common names. \"Not found\" means \"not found where we looked\", not \"missing\".</p></details>\r\n<details><summary>Can I check a supplier's domain?</summary><p>Yes. Enter your own work email and the supplier's domain. The records are public, and suppliers' accounts are a common route for payment fraud.</p></details>\r\n</section>\r\n<footer class=\"ic-foot\">\r\n<p>Product names such as Google, Microsoft, Proofpoint and Mimecast belong to their owners. They are named only because they appear in public DNS records; no affiliation or endorsement is implied. <a href=\"https://www.aegisai.com/privacy-policy\">Privacy policy</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Credits: personal email domain list based on <a href=\"https://github.com/willwhite/freemail\">freemail</a>, © 2015 Will White, ISC licence. Typefaces: Archivo, Public Sans and IBM Plex Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1.</p>\r\n</footer>\r\n</main></div>";
